ggml : the prefetch copies the experts the cache holds from VRAM

Phase 6b of docs/moe-offload-plan.md in EuLLM, on top of patch 0003. With
the prefetch, a 2048-token micro-batch of a long prompt takes as long as
the copy of its experts over PCIe 4.0 (33 GiB at 24 GB/s on
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ2_XS, 1.48 s); the GPU's computing is hidden under it.
The expert cache of PR #29887 keeps some of those experts in VRAM all the
while, and the prefetch copied them over the bus all the same.

ggml_backend_sched_set_moe_prefetch_lookup gives the scheduler a callback
that says, for a host expert tensor, which of its experts sit in a device
tensor and in which slot. The prefetch then fills a slot in runs: the
others over the bus on its copy stream, as before, and the experts the
cache holds by device-to-device copies from its bank, merging consecutive
experts where they are consecutive at both ends. llama.cpp sets the
callback where a context has both the cache and the prefetch
(llama_moe_cache::sched_lookup); the slot of a (layer, expert) is the
same in the banks of all of the layer's projections.

The copies from VRAM go on the GPU's own stream, queued when the slot's
previous reader already is: the stream's order puts them after it, and
after the cache's own copies into its banks for the steps before. Put on
the copy stream between the copies over the bus they held those up, and
reading a 33,200-token prompt went from 1,419 to 1,061 tokens/s. The cache
changes nothing while a graph of 512 tokens or more runs: it serves
batches of up to 32 tokens.

LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_FROM_CACHE=0 copies everything over the bus, as in 0003,
to compare. One line on stderr says the share of a micro-batch's bytes
taken from VRAM, the first time there is any.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp b11925, after 0003.

diff --git a/ggml/include/ggml-backend-prefetch.h b/ggml/include/ggml-backend-prefetch.h
index 73a0b3ee..70504eba 100644
--- a/ggml/include/ggml-backend-prefetch.h
+++ b/ggml/include/ggml-backend-prefetch.h
@@ -16,6 +16,16 @@ extern "C" {
     // else it needs and does not find turns it off with one line on stderr. Before any graph is allocated.
     GGML_API void ggml_backend_sched_set_moe_prefetch(ggml_backend_sched_t sched, int n_slots, int min_tokens);
 
+    // The experts of a host expert tensor that already sit in VRAM, which the prefetch then copies from
+    // there rather than over the bus. Returns false when none of src's experts is there; otherwise *bank
+    // is the device tensor that holds them, one expert every bank->nb[2] bytes, and slot_of[e] (src->ne[2]
+    // entries) the slot of expert e in it, or -1. Asked as a long prompt's micro-batch is queued, while
+    // what it holds does not change.
+    typedef bool (*ggml_backend_sched_moe_prefetch_lookup_t)(void * user_data, const struct ggml_tensor * src, const struct ggml_tensor ** bank, int32_t * slot_of);
+
+    // After ggml_backend_sched_set_moe_prefetch; nothing where that left the prefetch off.
+    GGML_API void ggml_backend_sched_set_moe_prefetch_lookup(ggml_backend_sched_t sched, ggml_backend_sched_moe_prefetch_lookup_t lookup, void * user_data);
+
 #ifdef  __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
